#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""agi-memguard (box-owner-S2-L5-V, owner 09-25 after the 04:00Z OOM took every seat down).
Every 5 s: a post's SPINE and HARNESS keep oom_score_adj -900 + nice -5, chosen by the post's cgroup
(/agi.slice/agi-post@*.service) AND their place in the unit's process tree, never by a command name: the spine is the chain
from the unit's oldest process down to the first process that has more than one child or a child whose argv is the tail of
its own (the tracer, and the harness is that child), plus everything the tracer runs that is not the harness; the harness's
DESCENDANTS (tool calls, MCP servers, kids) and anything orphaned out of the tree stay unprotected. tmux and the stream keep
-900 too (by command, outside the posts); every other pi worker gets +500 (the kernel kills them first);
a process over 70% of RAM, or the largest unprotected one when MemAvailable < 1 GiB, is SIGSTOPped (suspended, never killed), a
post's spine or harness over 70% only alerts (goal:g7.16.1.11.40.1);
a drop of >= 3 GiB within 30 s alerts. Alerts: journal + /var/log/agi-memguard.log (best effort: an unwritable log costs ONE red '[memguard-log] unwritable' line per episode, never a stop; the journal line is a fire-and-forget `timeout 30 logger` reaped through the pending list, never waited on and never fatal, so a slow journald or a missing logger cannot hold or kill a stop) + one line in the ~/.notice of each of sanctuary-master belam
(written BY that post's own uid through runuser, with its agi-notice when it has one: root signs nothing and holds no key; the file stays
the post's own; one line per kind per 600 s, but a stop or resume line is keyed by its pid too, so a second stop is never swallowed). Each of those alerts is ALSO ONE signed message to belam (goal:g7.16.1.11.20.2, council 3/3 21:3xZ): root appends a plain line, no key, to sanctuary-master's alarm spool by runuser as that seat, fire-and-forget like the notice, and the seat's own drain signs and sends it, exactly once. A pid stopped for
low memory is SIGCONTed once MemAvailable has stayed above 2x the low line for 30 s, and the notice line names its unit + pid;
a pid stopped for size is resumed by hand and says so again every 1800 s while it stays stopped.
The kernel is the one home of "stopped": every tick, before anything else reads the list, a pid whose /proc/N/stat state is not T/t (resumed by hand),
whose start time changed (the pid was reused) or that is gone is dropped from it with one journal line and no alert, with its cooldown keys.
A pid inside a post that is neither spine nor harness but carries the protect value or nice is a CHILD that inherited them (the kernel passes both to every fork): it goes back to its unit's own OOMScoreAdjust and Nice, read from systemd (cached 300 s), so a tool the harness runs stays an ordinary OOM and SIGSTOP candidate. The reset runs at the END of the tick, after every stop and resume path, and asks systemd nothing while MemAvailable is under the low line (a cached value still applies): a hung systemctl can never delay a SIGSTOP. Alerts of a kind that name a unit (tree, base) are rate-limited per unit. Each of the three alert-once sets (nobase, noh, unread) is an EPISODE: it leaves the set on the first good reading (the base read again, the harness found again, the tree read again), so a later real miss of the same unit says so again (still under the per-unit cooldown). The 'no harness' ALERT needs TWO consecutive ticks that find the SAME incarnation's tracer without a harness (goal:g7.16.1.11.40.1.2: the STOP window of an old incarnation, harness gone and cgroup not yet, fired it once per rotation): the first such tick is only remembered (a pending set, unit -> InvocationID), the second with the unchanged InvocationID alerts. The pending entry is cleared silently when the harness is found, and with ONE non-red line ('no harness for 1 tick, then the unit's cgroup emptied: a stop window', or '... the unit restarted ...') when the cgroup is gone, the unit is young again or its InvocationID changed. The InvocationID is ONE `systemctl show` for all candidate units, read at the tick END inside the one-fetch budget (a restart skips that tick's baseline read, never a SIGSTOP) and not at all while MemAvailable is under the low line (the 2-tick rule still holds there, with a no-id sentinel and the note 'judged under the low line, no InvocationID read': the one-fetch rule forbids the READ, never the judging); an InvocationID that cannot be read is judged AT ONCE (fail loud, like the uptime rule), and a tree that cannot be read stays the 'tree unreadable' ALERT on its first tick (the pending set never swallows an unread). A unit whose oldest process is younger than 2 ticks + 1 s (a restart in flight: its cgroup exists before its harness does) is not judged this tick: no 'no harness' / 'tree unreadable' line, no set entry, the next tick asks again; its spine is protected as always. That skip rests on three assumptions, each failing in a known direction: (1) a restart leaves no old process in the cgroup, true only while the post unit has KillMode=control-group and no harness respawns inside a live unit: under mixed or process the old incarnation's survivors make the oldest process look old, so a young unit IS judged (the old noise, a false 'no harness', never a silence); (2) the age is read from /proc/uptime, and if that cannot be read the unit IS judged (fail loud: the line fires); (3) a unit that crash-loops with lives shorter than that window is never judged by the tree rows at all, which is right only because NRestarts shows it. The two tree alerts keep their own cooldown keys (tree-noh-<unit>, tree-unread-<unit>): two faults on one unit never share one. systemd is asked for ONE unit baseline per tick, so a hung systemctl costs one 10 s timeout per tick, never one per unit.
The SUSPENDED line is written BEFORE the SIGSTOP is sent, but ONLY its local append to /var/log/agi-memguard.log is (no fork, no notice: the stop never waits on anything slow, the same rule as the inherited-nice reset); the journal line and the notice follow the SIGSTOP, and only when it succeeded. The line carries the pid's START TIME (`start N`, stat field 22), so restage and a2.undo never continue a REUSED pid. A stop killed between the line and the kill still leaves a line (the harmless direction; a line without a stop is read as 'resumed by hand' at the next tick), and a stop without a line, which nothing can find after a restart, cannot happen. If that append itself raises (disk full, EACCES) the pid is SIGSTOPped ANYWAY and one red journal + notice line says 'STOPPED WITHOUT a log line': restage and a2.undo cannot see that pid and the line names its resume command. If the signal itself fails the pid leaves the stopped map and one alert says it is NOT stopped (the SUSPENDED line stays in the file, no notice is sent for it). The tree selection reads argv only as the exact tail equality between one unit's tracer and its child: never a pattern, never printed."""
import os, re, time, signal, subprocess, collections
PAGE = os.sysconf('SC_PAGE_SIZE'); ME = os.getpid()
def meminfo(k): return int(re.search(rf'^{k}:\s+(\d+)', open('/proc/meminfo').read(), re.M).group(1)) * 1024
TOTAL = meminfo('MemTotal')
PROTECT_COMM = {'claude', 'tmux: server', 'ffmpeg', 'tmux'}
PROTECT_CMD = re.compile(r'streamer-stub|rotate\.py launch-wrapper|agi-memguard')
PI_CMD = re.compile(r'\.npm-global/(bin/pi\b|lib/node_modules/\S*pi)')
POST_CG = re.compile(r'^0::/agi\.slice/agi-post@[^/\n]+\.service(/|$)', re.M)
hist = collections.deque(); stopped = {}; base = {}; nobase = set(); warned = set(); noh = set(); pending = {}; unread = set(); last = {}; last_re = {}; pend = []; rec = None
SAFE = re.compile(r'^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$')
logbad = False
def wr(line):
    global logbad
    try: open('/var/log/agi-memguard.log', 'a').write(line + '\n'); logbad = False
    except Exception as e:
        if not logbad:
            logbad = True; m = f'[memguard-log] unwritable ({e!r}): /var/log/agi-memguard.log takes no lines until it is writable again; alerts still go to the journal and the notices'
            try: jlog(m); notice(m)
            except Exception: pass
def notice(text):
    for to in 'sanctuary-master belam'.split():
        if not SAFE.match(to): continue
        try:
            pend.append(subprocess.Popen(['timeout', '30', 'runuser', '-u', 'agi-' + to, '--', 'env', 'HOME=/var/lib/agi/' + to, 'sh', '-c',
                              '[ -x ~/bin/agi-notice ] && exec ~/bin/agi-notice add "$0" || echo "$0" >> ~/.notice', text],
                             stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL))
        except Exception as e: wr(f'notice to {to} not written: {e!r}')
def spool(text):                                                     # goal:g7.16.1.11.20.2: the alarm as a SIGNED message. Root signs nothing and holds no key: it APPENDS one plain line to the sending seat's spool by runuser as that seat (like the notice above), fire-and-forget; the seat's own drain row signs and sends it to the reader, exactly once. ONE line per alarm, not one per notice recipient
    seat = 'sanctuary-master'
    if not SAFE.match(seat): return
    try:
        pend.append(subprocess.Popen(['timeout', '30', 'runuser', '-u', 'agi-' + seat, '--', 'python3', '/opt/agi/bin/alarm_spool.py', 'append', '--job', 'memguard', '--to', 'belam',
                          '--max-lines', '500', '--spool', '/var/lib/agi/' + seat + '/alarm.spool', '--text', text],
                         stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL))
    except Exception as e: wr(f'alarm spool for {seat} not appended: {e!r}')
def jlog(msg):                                                       # the journal line, fire-and-forget like the notice: never waited on (a slow /dev/log must not hold a stop), never fatal (fork EAGAIN, logger missing), a hung logger is killed at 30 s and reaped through pend
    try: pend.append(subprocess.Popen(['timeout', '30', 'logger', '-t', 'agi-memguard', msg], stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL))
    except Exception as e: wr(f'journal line not written ({e!r}): {msg}')
def stamp(msg): return time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', time.gmtime()) + ' ' + msg
def log(msg, red=False, kind='x', key=None, wrote=False):
    if not wrote: wr(stamp(msg))
    jlog(msg)
    key = key or kind
    if red and time.time() - last.get(key, 0) > 600:
        last[key] = time.time()
        for k in [k for k, v in last.items() if len(last) > 200 and time.time() - v > 600]: del last[k]
        line = f'[memguard-{kind}] ' + msg + f' (ev {int(time.time()):08x})'
        notice(line); spool(line)
def unit_of(pid):
    try: return open(f'/proc/{pid}/cgroup').read().strip().split('\n')[-1].rsplit('/', 1)[-1] or '?'
    except Exception: return '?'
def procs():
    for d in os.listdir('/proc'):
        if not d.isdigit() or int(d) in (1, ME): continue
        try:
            comm = open(f'/proc/{d}/comm').read().strip(); cmd = open(f'/proc/{d}/cmdline').read().replace('\0', ' ')
            rss = int(open(f'/proc/{d}/statm').read().split()[1]) * PAGE
        except Exception: continue
        if cmd: yield int(d), comm, cmd, rss
def post_rows(snap):
    out = {}
    for pid, comm, cmd, rss in snap:
        try:
            m = POST_CG.search(open(f'/proc/{pid}/cgroup').read()); s = open(f'/proc/{pid}/stat').read()
            if m: r = s[s.rindex(')') + 2:].split(); out.setdefault(m.group(0).rstrip('/'), {})[pid] = (int(r[1]), int(r[19]), cmd)
        except Exception: pass
    return out
def guarded(rows):
    kids = collections.defaultdict(list)
    for p, (pp, st, c) in rows.items(): kids[pp].append(p)
    n = min((p for p, (pp, st, c) in rows.items() if pp not in rows), key=lambda p: rows[p][1]); chain = [n]; h = None
    while not h:
        h = max((k for k in kids[n] if rows[k][2].strip() and rows[n][2].endswith(rows[k][2])), key=lambda k: len(rows[k][2]), default=None)
        if h or len(kids[n]) != 1: break
        n = kids[n][0]; chain.append(n)
    out = set(chain)
    def sub(p): return {p}.union(*(sub(k) for k in kids[p]))
    if h:
        out.add(h)
        for k in kids[n]:
            if k != h: out |= sub(k)
    return out, bool(h)
def pstat(pid):
    try: s = open(f'/proc/{pid}/stat').read(); r = s[s.rindex(')') + 2:].split(); return r[0], r[19]
    except Exception: return None
HZ = os.sysconf('SC_CLK_TCK'); YOUNG_S = 2 * 5 + 1; fetched = False
def young(rows):
    try: return float(open('/proc/uptime').read().split()[0]) - min(v[1] for v in rows.values()) / HZ < YOUNG_S
    except Exception: return False
def cleared(unit, why):
    if unit in pending: del pending[unit]; log(f'{unit}: no harness for 1 tick, then {why}: a stop window')
def invocations(units):
    global fetched
    fetched = True; got = {}
    try:
        for blk in subprocess.check_output(['systemctl', 'show', *[u.rsplit('/', 1)[-1] for u in units], '-p', 'Id', '-p', 'InvocationID'], text=True, timeout=10, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL).split('\n\n'):
            kv = dict(l.split('=', 1) for l in blk.split('\n') if '=' in l)
            if kv.get('Id') and kv.get('InvocationID'): got[kv['Id']] = kv['InvocationID']
    except Exception: pass
    return got
def baseline(unit, now, fetch):
    global fetched
    b = base.get(unit)
    if fetch and not fetched and (b is None or now - b[2] >= 300):
        fetched = True
        try:
            kv = dict(l.split('=', 1) for l in subprocess.check_output(['systemctl', 'show', unit, '-p', 'OOMScoreAdjust', '-p', 'Nice'], text=True, timeout=10, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL).split('\n') if '=' in l)
            b = (int(kv['OOMScoreAdjust']), int(kv['Nice']), now); nobase.discard(unit)
        except Exception as e:
            b = (None, None, now)
            if unit not in nobase: nobase.add(unit); log(f'ALERT {unit}: its OOMScoreAdjust and Nice could not be read ({e!r}): a child that inherited the protect value stays protected', red=True, kind='base', key=f'base-{unit}')
        base[unit] = b
    return b or (None, None, 0)
def unprotect(pid, unit, now, fetch):
    try: adj = int(open(f'/proc/{pid}/oom_score_adj').read()); nice = os.getpriority(os.PRIO_PROCESS, pid)
    except Exception: return
    if adj != -900 and nice != -5: return
    a, n, _ = baseline(unit, now, fetch)
    if a is None: return
    if adj == -900: setadj(pid, a)
    if nice == -5:
        try: os.setpriority(os.PRIO_PROCESS, pid, n)
        except Exception: pass
def sigstop(pid, comm):
    try: os.kill(pid, signal.SIGSTOP); return True
    except Exception as e:
        stopped.pop(pid, None); log(f'ALERT pid {pid} ({comm}): the SIGSTOP failed ({e!r}), it is NOT stopped: the SUSPENDED line in /var/log/agi-memguard.log was written first', red=True, kind=f'stopfail-{pid}'); return False
def suspend(pid, comm, kind, now, text):
    u = unit_of(pid); st = (pstat(pid) or ('', ''))[1]; stopped[pid] = (kind, comm, u, now, st); msg = text(u, st); err = None
    try: open('/var/log/agi-memguard.log', 'a').write(stamp(msg) + '\n')         # the ONLY thing before the SIGSTOP: a local append, no fork, no notice (restage and a2.undo scan this file)
    except Exception as e: err = e                                       # a full disk or EACCES must not cost the stop: the runaway keeps allocating
    if sigstop(pid, comm):
        if err is None: log(msg, red=True, kind=f'susp-{pid}', key=f'susp-{pid}-{st}', wrote=True)       # then the journal and the notice, which fork and may crawl under the very reclaim that made the guard act
        else: log(f'ALERT pid {pid} ({comm}) STOPPED WITHOUT a log line ({err!r}): restage and a2.undo cannot see it -- kill -CONT {pid}', red=True, kind=f'susp-{pid}', key=f'susp-{pid}-{st}', wrote=True)
def setadj(pid, v):
    try:
        p = f'/proc/{pid}/oom_score_adj'
        if int(open(p).read()) != v: open(p, 'w').write(str(v))
    except Exception: pass
while True:
    now = time.time(); avail = meminfo('MemAvailable'); hist.append((now, avail)); pend[:] = [q for q in pend if q.poll() is None]
    while hist and now - hist[0][0] > 30: hist.popleft()
    peak = max(a for _, a in hist)
    if peak - avail >= 3 << 30: log(f'SPIKE: MemAvailable fell {(peak-avail)>>20} MiB in <=30 s, now {avail>>20} MiB', red=True, kind='spike'); hist.clear(); hist.append((now, avail))
    unprot = []; fetched = False; snap = list(procs()); inpost = set(); keep = set(); pu = {}; late = []; cand = []
    for p in list(stopped):
        st = pstat(p)
        if st is None or st[0] not in 'Tt' or st[1] != stopped[p][4]:
            log(f'pid {p} ({stopped[p][1]}) ' + ('gone' if st is None else 'resumed by hand' if st[1] == stopped[p][4] else 'is a different process now (pid reused)') + ': no longer tracked as stopped')
            was = stopped.pop(p); last_re.pop(p, None)
            for k in ('susp', 'resume', 'still'): last.pop(f'{k}-{p}-{was[4]}', None)
    posts = post_rows(snap)
    for unit in [u for u in pending if u not in posts]: cleared(unit, "the unit's cgroup emptied")
    for unit, rows in posts.items():
        inpost |= set(rows); pu.update((p, unit.rsplit('/', 1)[-1]) for p in rows)
        try:
            g, found = guarded(rows); keep |= g; unread.discard(unit)
            if found: noh.discard(unit); pending.pop(unit, None)
            elif unit in noh: pass
            elif young(rows): cleared(unit, 'the unit restarted')
            else: cand.append(unit)
        except Exception as e:
            pending.pop(unit, None)
            if unit not in unread and not young(rows): unread.add(unit); log(f'ALERT {unit}: the process tree could not be read ({e!r}): nothing in it is protected this tick', red=True, kind='tree', key=f'tree-unread-{unit}')
    for pid, comm, cmd, rss in snap:
        prot = pid in keep or (pid not in inpost and (comm in PROTECT_COMM or bool(PROTECT_CMD.search(cmd))))
        if prot:
            setadj(pid, -900)
            try:
                if os.getpriority(os.PRIO_PROCESS, pid) > -5: os.setpriority(os.PRIO_PROCESS, pid, -5)
            except Exception: pass
        elif PI_CMD.search(cmd):
            setadj(pid, 500)
            if pid in pu: late.append((pid, pu[pid]))               # a worker keeps its adj, but a nice it inherited from the harness is reset like any child's
        elif pid in pu: late.append((pid, pu[pid]))
        if not prot: unprot.append((rss, pid, comm))
        if pid in keep and rss > 0.70 * TOTAL and pid not in warned:
            warned.add(pid); log(f'ALERT pid {pid} ({comm}) is a post\'s spine or harness: RSS {rss>>20} MiB > 70% of {TOTAL>>20} MiB -- not stopped', red=True, kind='post')
        elif pid not in keep and rss > 0.70 * TOTAL and pid not in stopped:
            suspend(pid, comm, 'size', now, lambda u, st: f'SUSPENDED pid {pid} ({comm}, unit {u}, start {st}): RSS {rss>>20} MiB > 70% of {TOTAL>>20} MiB -- resume by hand: kill -CONT {pid}')
    if avail < 1 << 30 and unprot:
        rss, pid, comm = max(unprot)
        if pid not in stopped:
            suspend(pid, comm, 'low', now, lambda u, st: f'SUSPENDED pid {pid} ({comm}, unit {u}, start {st}, RSS {rss>>20} MiB): MemAvailable {avail>>20} MiB < 1 GiB -- resumed automatically once MemAvailable holds above 2x that for 30 s, or by hand: kill -CONT {pid}')
    lows = [p for p, v in stopped.items() if v[0] == 'low']
    if lows and avail > 2 * (1 << 30):
        rec = rec or now
        if now - rec >= 30:
            for p in lows:
                try: os.kill(p, signal.SIGCONT); how = 'resumed'
                except Exception as e: how = f'could not resume ({e!r})'
                log(f'RESUMED pid {p} ({stopped[p][1]}, unit {stopped[p][2]}): {how}; MemAvailable {avail>>20} MiB held above 2x the low line for 30 s', red=True, kind=f'resume-{p}', key=f'resume-{p}-{stopped[p][4]}'); del stopped[p]
            rec = None
    else: rec = None
    for p, v in stopped.items():
        if v[0] == 'size' and now - last_re.setdefault(p, v[3]) >= 1800:
            last_re[p] = now; log(f'STILL STOPPED pid {p} ({v[1]}, unit {v[2]}) for {int(now - v[3]) // 60} min (size stop): resume by hand: kill -CONT {p}', red=True, kind=f'still-{p}', key=f'still-{p}-{v[4]}')
    if cand:
        low = avail < 1 << 30; ids = {} if low else invocations(cand)          # the 2-tick rule holds at ANY memory level; only the systemd READ waits out the low line
        for unit in cand:
            i = None if low else ids.get(unit.rsplit('/', 1)[-1]); p = pending.get(unit)
            if not low and not i: pending.pop(unit, None); noh.add(unit); why = ' (its InvocationID could not be read: judged at once)'
            elif p is None: pending[unit] = i or ''; continue                                       # the first tick: remembered ('' = no InvocationID read)
            elif i and p and p != i: cleared(unit, 'the unit restarted'); pending[unit] = i; continue
            else: pending.pop(unit, None); noh.add(unit); why = ' (judged under the low line, no InvocationID read)' if low else '' if p else ' (its first tick was judged under the low line, no InvocationID read)'
            log(f'ALERT {unit}: no harness found under its tracer (its argv is not the tail of the tracer\'s): only the spine chain is protected' + why, red=True, kind='tree', key=f'tree-noh-{unit}')
    for pid, unit in late: unprotect(pid, unit, now, avail >= 1 << 30)
    warned = {p for p in warned if os.path.exists(f'/proc/{p}')}
    time.sleep(5)
